# Build-context exclusions for every image built with `context: .` (the root-module Go services and
# tools). Docker reads .dockerignore from the ROOT OF THE BUILD CONTEXT, so this file does nothing
# for the frontend (context: ./frontend — it has its own) or viz-gateway (context: services/viz-gateway).
#
# Patterns are anchored at the context root unless prefixed with **/. The old `node_modules` line
# matched only a top-level directory, so frontend/node_modules (hundreds of MB on a developer box)
# was uploaded to the daemon on every local build of every Go image.
.git
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.proof-logs
**/*.md
!**/README.md
local_data_dir
frontend/
docs/
truth/
.claude/
.claude-flow/
.github/
scripts/
*.docx
